### What should a senior engineer know?

A senior engineer recognises this as a problem-inversion pattern that appears in many graph problems. The idea of marking the complement and capturing the rest applies to boundary-connected component problems in image processing, game of life variants, and territory control. They also know that using a sentinel in-place saves memory over a separate visited matrix, and that BFS is safer for production-sized boards.

```java
package com.bank.service;

public class SeniorSurroundedNotes {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Senior insights:");
        System.out.println("  1. Problem inversion: mark complement, capture rest.");
        System.out.println("  2. Sentinel saves memory over visited matrix.");
        System.out.println("  3. BFS safer for large boards (no stack overflow).");
        System.out.println("  4. Time: O(rows * cols), Space: O(rows * cols) worst case.");
    }
}
```
